Summary of Supervised vs. Unsupervised Learning:
​Supervised Learning is like learning with a teacher. The system is trained on a dataset where the correct answers (labels) are already known. 
The goal is to learn a mapping from inputs to outputs.
Common uses include Spam Filtering (Classification) and House Price Prediction (Regression).
Unsupervised Learning is like learning without a teacher. The system is given data with no labels and must find structure on its own.
It is commonly used for Customer Segmentation (Clustering) or finding unusual patterns (Anomaly Detection).
